---
import ProductLayout from '../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
---
<ProductLayout title="Security — ExpenseTracking | Facware" description="Security practices, data controls, and vulnerability reporting for ExpenseTracking." canonicalURL="https://web-expense-tracking.facware.com/security.html" currentPage="security">
  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-container">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Trust center</p>
      <h1>Security and data controls</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: October 7, 2026</p>
      <p>ExpenseTracking is designed to keep local use simple and minimize the amount of financial information that leaves your device.</p>
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul><li>Serve the public portal over HTTPS.</li><li>Keep local-first use available without a Facware account.</li><li>Request Google permissions only for an enabled backup or restore feature.</li><li>Do not sell transaction data or use Google Drive data for advertising.</li><li>Provide export, deletion, and Google access-revocation paths.</li></ul>
      <h2>What you should do</h2>
      <ul><li>Keep your device, browser, and Google Account protected with a strong password and multi-factor authentication.</li><li>Review the Google consent screen before enabling Drive.</li><li>Keep an independent export of important records.</li><li>Revoke Drive access if you no longer use backup.</li></ul>
      <h2>Report a vulnerability</h2>
      <p>Please report suspected security issues privately to <a href="mailto:contact@facware.com">contact@facware.com</a>. Include the affected URL or feature, steps to reproduce, impact, and a safe way to contact you. Do not include real financial records, access tokens, passwords, or other sensitive data in a report.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</ProductLayout>
